# moth.wasm (DESIGN §144): Moth's compiler as a WebAssembly module of its own. This program is it: compiler.moth
# reads a program, and wasm.moth makes it into the module moth build --target wasm makes. make-moth-wasm.mjs
# builds it into moth.wasm, by itself; the playground compiles with it.
#
# It's run with the program's text and the files it may use as its arguments: the text, then each file's name and
# text. It says one line: the module's bytes, each a number, with what running it needs in its section "moth"; or,
# for a mistake in the program, "mistake" and the mistake as JSON, its place and its reason.

use "wasm.moth" as webassembly

set moth_given to arguments
set moth_names to empty list
set moth_texts to empty list
set moth_k to 2
repeat while moth_k is less than length of moth_given
    add item moth_k of moth_given to moth_names
    add item (moth_k + 1) of moth_given to moth_texts
    set moth_k to moth_k + 2
end
try
    set moth_made to webassembly's wasm_compile(item 1 of moth_given, moth_names, moth_texts)
    say join webassembly's wasm_with_details(moth_made) with ","
if it fails with moth_why
    say "mistake " + (moth_why as json)
end
